          "question": "Burning when I pee and going more often since yesterday, no temperature.",
          "answer": "You've described burning during urination and increased frequency of urination. These symptoms often involve the urinary system.\n\nA common condition associated with these symptoms is a lower urinary tract infection. This type of infection can cause burning or pain when you urinate, as well as needing to go more often. Unlike an upper urinary tract infection, a lower tract infection typically does not involve a fever (condition-urinary-tract-infection).\n\nIt is important to discuss these symptoms with a clinician to determine the cause and appropriate steps.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
